Real-time kanban board with Go, Gin, and Supabase.

Tasks are stored in Supabase Postgres. Row Level Security (RLS) is enabled by
the migration in `supabase/migrations`; requests must include a Supabase user
access token so PostgREST evaluates policies as that user.
Database access uses the official
[`supabase-community/supabase-go`](https://github.com/supabase-community/supabase-go)
client and its PostgREST query builder.

## API

- `GET /users/:user_id/tasks` lists tasks for a user.
- `POST /tasks` creates a task.
- `GET /tasks/:task_id` gets a task by ID.
- `POST /auth/guest` creates an anonymous Supabase user and returns its session.
- `POST /auth/refresh` refreshes an existing session.
- `PATCH /tasks/:task_id` updates an owned task.
- `POST /auth/link` requests email confirmation for the current guest.
- `GET /swagger/index.html` opens Swagger UI.

Open Swagger UI at [http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html](http://localhost:8080/swagger/index.html).
Click **Authorize** and enter `Bearer <Supabase user access token>` to test
the protected endpoints.

To start without an account, call `POST /auth/guest` without an
`Authorization` header. Store the returned `access_token`, then use it as
`Bearer <access_token>` for task requests. To start saving the guest, call
`POST /auth/link` with that bearer token and:

```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}
```

After email confirmation, POST /auth/password with { "password": "..." } to set a password. GET /auth/account returns current account state. POST /auth/login signs in an existing account.

Enable anonymous sign-ins in Supabase Auth before using the guest endpoint.
The task routes are intentionally token-protected because their RLS policies
need the authenticated user's JWT; the guest-session route is public.

## Next.js integration handoff

Architecture: Browser -> Next.js session/proxy routes -> Gin -> Supabase.

This repository owns Supabase clients, database access, business validation,
authentication, token refresh, and all database migrations. Next.js owns the UI,
an encrypted HttpOnly session cookie, and authenticated proxy routes. Supabase
credentials do not belong in Next.js.

- POST /auth/guest creates a guest only when Next.js has no session cookie.
- POST /auth/refresh accepts { "refresh_token": "..." } from the trusted Next.js
  server and returns the refreshed Supabase session. Invalid tokens return 401;
  upstream service failures return 502. Never expose this response to browser JS.
- POST /auth/link links the current bearer-authenticated guest to email/password.
- PATCH /tasks/:task_id updates title, description, status, and priority. Unknown
  fields (including user_id) and invalid values are rejected. Database requests
  use the caller's JWT; Supabase RLS limits updates to that user's own tasks.

Next.js forwards task requests with Authorization: Bearer <access_token>,
refreshes before expiry, and stores rotated tokens in its encrypted cookie.
Never replace a failed session with a new guest automatically.

Configure SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY in this repository's .env.
Enable Supabase anonymous sign-ins. Apply migrations from supabase/migrations
in filename order using the Supabase SQL editor or migration tooling. The migrations create the tasks table, enforce owner-only RLS policies, and
add authenticated-role grants and a lookup index.
Never use a secret/service-role key to handle user task requests.

Frontend configuration consists only of KANBAN_BACKEND_URL and SESSION_SECRET.
After changing backend routes, restart Gin. Swagger documents the update and
refresh routes at /swagger/index.html.

## Run

```powershell
go run .
```

```powershell
go test ./...
```

## Integration tests

Run go test ./... for endpoint validation, JWT forwarding, update behavior, and
refresh handling against an in-process mock provider. To exercise the configured
live Supabase project, set KANBAN_LIVE_TEST=1 and run go test ./... . The live
test checks persistence, user isolation, and refresh, and removes its own task.

## Collaboration

See COLLABORATION.md for the request flow, SSE synchronization, permissions, and validation.
The collaborative endpoints are implemented in kanban/collaboration.go; SQL lives in supabase/migrations.
Run go test ./... and supabase/tests/email_invitations.sql (transactional rollback) for regression checks.
Invitations target verified email addresses and appear in the recipient workspace. No outbound email is sent. Gin subscribes to Supabase Realtime Postgres Changes and relays SSE.
